    "verdict": "Against paper ref 8's own series — our core with an imidazole N-donor, [Os(X2-bpy)2(PVI)Cl]+ at one loading, pH 7.4 — per 4,4'-substituent: OMe−H -60.9 ours against -70.0 measured (×0.87); Me−H -37.2 ours against -27.7 measured (×1.34); Cl−H +41.9 ours against +17.2 measured (×2.43); OMe−Me -23.6 ours against -42.2 measured (×0.56); Cl−Me +79.1 ours against +45.0 measured (×1.76); Cl−OMe +102.8 ours against +87.2 measured (×1.18). The measured sensitivity falls from the donor to the acceptor side and ours much less (pairwise slopes, V/σ per substituent — ome-dmbpy: 0.422 measured, 0.236 ours; dmbpy-bpy: 0.163 measured, 0.219 ours; bpy-cl: 0.075 measured, 0.182 ours), so the computed effect is about right for OMe against H and too large toward the acceptor end. The same Me complex from another source at another loading sits +135 mV away (A5) — more than all four Me → H — so the film and its preparation move E°′ by more than the pairs compared, and only the equal-loading points of one route are compared."
