      "verdict": "Relaxing Os(III) as well, from each relaxed Os(II) geometry (adiabatic ΔSCF, λ_III 86–110 meV; no free energies). The 6 donor rows the three measured series share with it rest on three computed pairs, two of them independent (OMe−Me = OMe−H − Me−H). Against Os(III) kept vertical: Me−H +6.1 mV (closer in ref 8, MeCN), OMe−H +4.2 mV (closer in ref 8, MeCN), OMe−Me -1.9 mV (away in ref 8, aqueous); against the programmatic geometry: Me−H +9.3 mV (closer in ref 8, MeCN), OMe−H -10.8 mV (closer in ref 8; away in MeCN), OMe−Me -20.1 mV (closer in ref 8, aqueous). Ref 8's films — our core and N-donor — OMe−H ×0.87 → ×1.08 → ×1.02; Me−H ×1.34 → ×1.23 → ×1.01; OMe−Me ×0.56 → ×0.99 → ×1.04 (|ours − measured| at most 1.7 mV per substituent with both states relaxed); the aqueous OMe−Me ×0.59 → ×1.05 → ×1.10; the homoleptic MeCN OMe−H ×0.99 → ×1.23 → ×1.16, Me−H ×2.48 → ×2.27 → ×1.86. From the programmatic geometry the donor pairs move by up to 20.1 mV per substituent (OMe−Me, 80 meV a complex) and the points by -26 to +54 meV; the Koopmans cascade Δ of each relaxed member moves by -0.142 eV (OMe), -0.070 eV (Me), -0.091 eV (H) with Os(III) on its own minimum (up to 0.142 eV over both Os(III) geometries), and stays monotonic in σ over the relaxed donors on both Os(III) geometries — where the programmatic gaps are 84 meV or more; the closest neighbours of Table 4 are not relaxed in both members (NMe₂→NH₂ 1.5 meV, NO₂→SO₂CF₃ 5.0 meV, COOH→CF₃ 40.0 meV). On its own minimum Os(III) takes Os–Cl back from 2.522–2.533 to 2.416–2.428 Å. By the letter of D's first trigger (0.1 eV), the Koopmans cascade Δ of OMe reaches it; the slope ①, extrapolated from the donors' +13 % over the LFER fit set's span (0.97 eV), moves by ≈0.13 eV — an extrapolation, not a computation. Whether a difference at the threshold carries a conclusion is D's to judge. Not relaxed in both states: NMe₂, NH₂, COOH, CF₃, SO₂CF₃."
    },
